# Images: an Image of a PDF draws one of its pages, chosen with PDF page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Images · PDF page
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: sheet
			Box:
				Width: 100%
				Border: 0.5
				Border color: rule
	Section:
		Text: Images
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: PDF page
		Paragraph: The page of a PDF goes in as a vector drawing, at the size of that page. `PDF page` chooses it, from 1, the first one by default. The file here has two pages, the letterhead of the first sheet and that of the following ones.
			Style: intro
		Grid:
			Column sizes: 225 225
			Gap: 6 24
			Area:
				Text: PDF page: 1  (the default)
					Style: label
			Area:
				Text: PDF page: 2
					Style: label
			Area:
				Image: examples/letterhead/letterhead.pdf
					Alt: Letterhead of the first sheet
					Style: sheet
			Area:
				Image: examples/letterhead/letterhead.pdf
					Alt: Letterhead of the following sheets
					Style: sheet
					PDF page: 2
